### Lab 11 test requests (VS Code "REST Client" extension, or copy into Postman)

### Courses with free seats (and, after Exercise 4, room / day / tags)
GET http://localhost:3000/courses

### Exercise 4 - filter on a JSON field
GET http://localhost:3000/courses?day=Mon

### Exercise 3 - students with their course count (stored function)
GET http://localhost:3000/students

### A student's enrolments
GET http://localhost:3000/students/9/enrolments

### Exercise 3 - enrol student 9 in course 3 (CALL enrol_student + trigger)
POST http://localhost:3000/students/9/enrolments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "course_id": 3 }

### Exercise 3 - cancel it (the delete trigger gives the seat back)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/students/9/enrolments/3

### Exercise 3 - duplicate enrolment: student 1 is already in course 1 (expect 409)
POST http://localhost:3000/students/1/enrolments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "course_id": 1 }

### Exercise 2/3 - a full course (first run: UPDATE courses SET seats = 0 WHERE id = 5;) -> 409 course is full
POST http://localhost:3000/students/9/enrolments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "course_id": 5 }

### Exercise 5 - reviews in the document store
GET http://localhost:3000/courses/1/reviews

###
POST http://localhost:3000/courses/1/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{ "student": "Ploy", "stars": 5, "comment": "Great labs", "tags": ["labs", "sql"] }
